/-!
# Stacks Tag 01VS: the morphism to projective space from ampleness, and four named inputs

Stacks Tag 01VS (Morphisms, Lemma 29.40.3) says that an ample invertible sheaf `L` on a scheme
`X` locally of finite type over `S` has all sufficiently high powers of the form `i ^* 𝒪(1)` for
an immersion `i : X ⟶ ℙⁿ_S` over `S`. The source proves it in seven steps; this file performs
steps 1 and 3 and names the rest, in the shape the source's own argument has.

## The steps of the source

1. The affine `X_a`, for `a` homogeneous of positive degree in the section ring, form a basis, so
   finitely many cover `X`, each mapping into an affine open of `S` — Properties, Proposition
   28.27.13, [Stacks, Tag 01Q3]. `Stacks.SectionExtension.exists_common_degree_affine_cover`
   produces the finite family, in one common degree `N`, with each `X_{a_i}` an affine open of `X`
   covering `X`, and `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.exists_generating_family_of_isAmple` packages
   that as a generating family for the next step. That statement does not contain the clause that
   each `X_{a_i}` maps into an affine open of `S` — its signature mentions no base scheme at all —
   and that clause is what step 2 needs, so it is part of `ChartImmersion` below. Refining the
   cover to achieve it is again ampleness, which `ChartImmersion` hypothesises.
2. The ring maps `𝒪_S(V_i) → 𝒪_X(X_{a_i})` are of finite type — [Stacks, Tag 01T2] — so the
   algebra generators can be written as ratios `a_{ij} / a_i^{e_{ij}}` by [Stacks, Tag 01PW].
   This is part of `ChartImmersion` below.
3. The degree-`N` elements generate `L ^⊗ N` and so define `j : X ⟶ ℙᵐ_S` with
   `j ^* 𝒪(1) = L ^⊗ N` — Constructions, Lemma 27.13.1, [Stacks, Tag 01NE]. The morphism is
   `exists_generating_hom_of_isAmple`, from ampleness alone, obtained by feeding
   `exists_generating_family_of_isAmple` to
   `Stacks.ProjGlobalSectionsAppTop.exists_hom_projectiveSpaceOver_of_generatesStalks`. The
   identification `j ^* 𝒪(1) = L ^⊗ N` is `TwistPullback` below.
4. Comparing coordinates, `j⁻¹(D₊(T_i)) = X_{a_i}` and `j` is a closed immersion into an affine
   open on each chart, hence an immersion. This is the conclusion of `ChartImmersion`.
5. `L ^⊗ d` is generated by finitely many global sections for every `d ≥ d₁` ([Stacks, Tag 01Q3]
   clause (7) again). This is `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers`.
6.–7. For `d ≥ d₀ = d₁ + N`, the products of the degree-`N` family with a generating family of
   `L ^⊗ (d − N)` generate `L ^⊗ d`, and the morphism they define factors as the pair `(j, j')`
   followed by the Segre embedding, so it is an immersion. The pair step is
   `Stacks.AmpleProjectiveImmersion.isImmersion_lift` and the Segre embedding is
   `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreProdIso.exists_segreEmbedding`, which hypothesises nothing
   beyond the base scheme. Neither asserts the identification of `𝒪(1)` along the Segre
   embedding; the whole of steps 6–7 is isolated as `TwistPassage` below.

## The degree cannot be fixed in advance

The condition *for every invertible `M` carrying a generating family of global sections with
affine nonvanishing opens, `M` is `i ^* 𝒪(1)` for an immersion `i : X ⟶ ℙⁿ_S` over `S`* is false,
in two ways.

* It carries **no finite type hypothesis**. For `X = Spec k[x₁, x₂, …]`, `S = Spec k`, `M = 𝒪_X`
  and the family `(1, 0)` — generating, both nonvanishing opens affine — the conclusion produces
  an immersion `X ⟶ ℙⁿ_k` over `k`, and `ℙⁿ_k` is of finite type over `k`, so `X` would be
  locally of finite type over `k`. It is not. Tag 01VS is false without its finite type
  hypothesis, so no reduction of it may discard that hypothesis.
* Adding the finite type hypothesis does **not** repair it. For `E` an elliptic curve over `k`
  and `M = 𝒪_E(2P)`: `M` is base point free, hence generating, and each `X_{sᵢ}` is the
  complement of an effective divisor on a projective curve, hence affine. An immersion out of a
  proper scheme is a closed immersion, so the conclusion says `𝒪_E(2P)` is very ample; a degree
  two embedded curve is a plane conic, of genus `0`. Note that `E` carries the ample `L = 𝒪_E(P)`
  and `M = L ^⊗ 2`, so the condition fails already for a power of an ample sheaf.

The error is a degree error, and it is the source's step 2 that pins the degree: the `N` of step 3
is a **common multiple of the degrees** of the `a_i` and of the `a_{ij}` that Tag 01PW produces,
so steps 2–4 deliver the twist for `M ^⊗ N` and not for `M`. A condition quantified over every
invertible `M` and concluding at `M` itself asserts the case `N = 1` of this, uniformly, and that
is exactly what fails on the elliptic curve. Likewise the source needs the charts affine only at
the single degree of step 1, where ampleness supplies them, and asks nothing of them in steps 5–7.

## The four named inputs

No input below mentions a tensor power, a degree bound and ampleness together, and none is Tag
01VS.

* `TwistPullback f`: **the twist half of Tag 01NE.** A morphism to `ℙⁿ_S` pinned on every chart by
  a generating family of global sections of `M` pulls `𝒪(1)` back to `M`. No ampleness, no finite
  type, no immersion, no degree.
* `ChartImmersion f L`: **steps 2 and 4.** From ampleness and finite type, some positive power of
  `L` carries a generating family whose pinned morphism is an immersion. It says nothing about
  `𝒪(1)` and nothing about any degree other than the one it produces.
* `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers X L`: **step 5** — half (1) of clause
  (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3], which is clause (7) at `F = 𝒪_X`. It mentions no morphism, no
  projective space and no immersion. It follows from clause (5) of the same tag
  (`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_clauseFive`), and holds in one positive
  degree by `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule`.
* `TwistPassage f L`: **steps 6 and 7.** If `L ^⊗ a` is `𝒪(1)` pulled back along an immersion over
  `S` and `L ^⊗ b` is generated by finitely many global sections, then so is `L ^⊗ (a + b)` for
  some immersion. No ampleness, no finite type and no degree bound occurs in it.

**The first two inputs together are strictly weaker than Tag 01VS**, and not by a wide margin:
they give the single-degree conclusion (`hasImmersionTwistOver_of_isAmple`), which the source
itself says "is enough in virtually all applications". The passage from one degree to all
`d ≥ d₀` is the separate content of the last two inputs, exactly as in the source.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.TwistPullback`: the twist half of Tag 01NE.
* `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.ChartImmersion`: steps 2 and 4 of the source.
* `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.TwistPassage`: steps 6 and 7 of the source.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.exists_generating_hom_of_isAmple`: **from ampleness alone, one
  degree `N ≥ 1` and a morphism `X ⟶ ℙⁿ_S` over `S` defined by a generating family of global
  sections of `L ^⊗ N` whose nonvanishing opens are affine**, with the morphism pinned on every
  chart. This is step 3 of the source.
* `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.locallyOfFiniteType_of_hasImmersionTwistOver`: **Tag 01VS's
  conclusion at a single degree implies Tag 01VS's own finite type hypothesis**, which is the
  first of the two counterexamples above.
* `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.hasImmersionTwistOver_of_isAmple`: **Tag 01VS at a single
  degree**, from `TwistPullback` and `ChartImmersion`.
* `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.hasImmersionTwistOver_multiples_of_isAmple`: **Tag 01VS in every
  degree `N + d k`**, from three of the four inputs — the eventual generation of the powers is not
  used, because it holds in one positive degree
  (`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule`).
* `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.immersionTwistGap_of_chartImmersionTwist`: **the whole of
  `Stacks.AmpleProjectiveImmersion.ImmersionTwistGap`** — hence the whole of Tag 01VS — from the
  four named inputs.
* `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.exists_immersion_projectiveSpaceOver_of_isAmple`: the statement
  of Tag 01VS, from the four named inputs.

## Implementation notes

**The inputs are stated about a pinned morphism, not about an existential.** The morphism of step
3 is constructed here, so `TwistPullback` and `ChartImmersion` quantify over every
`p : X ⟶ ℙⁿ_S` lying over `S` and restricting on each chart `X_{sᵢ}` to the explicit chart
morphism, and assert the twist and the immersion property of it. Nothing is therefore
re-existentialised, and the two inputs can be instantiated at the *same* morphism — the one
`Stacks.ProjGlobalSectionsAppTop.exists_hom_projectiveSpaceOver_of_generatesStalks` produces.

**Degrees are integers throughout.** `IsEventuallyFinGenPowers` is stated over `ℤ`, and keeping
the other inputs over `ℤ` means the bookkeeping in
`immersionTwistGap_of_chartImmersionTwist` is `N + (d - N) = d` in `ℤ` with no truncated
subtraction anywhere; the only cast is the one that turns the statement's `d₀ : ℕ` into a bound
on the integer degrees.

Tag 01NE is a representability statement; only its morphism is used here, with its twist
identification isolated as an input.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01VS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01T2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01T2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WD)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.Ample Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections Stacks.AmpleProjectiveImmersion
open Stacks.SectionsToProjectiveSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction

/-! ### Step 3 of the source: the morphism, from ampleness -/

section Morphism

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- **From ampleness alone: a degree, a generating family, and the morphism to projective space
over the base that it defines.**

This is step 3 of the proof of Stacks Tag 01VS. The last clause pins the morphism on each chart
`X_{sᵢ}`, so nothing about it is left to choice.

The identification `j ^* 𝒪(1) = L ^⊗ N`, which step 3 of the source also asserts, is not part of
this statement; it is `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.TwistPullback`. -/
theorem exists_generating_hom_of_isAmple (hL : IsAmple X L) {S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (n : ℕ) (s : Fin (n + 1) → Γ(tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ), ⊤))
      (p : X ⟶ projectiveSpaceOver n S),
      1 ≤ N ∧ GeneratesStalks s ∧ (∀ i, IsAffineOpen (nvCover s i)) ∧
        p ≫ pullback.fst (terminal.from S)
          (terminal.from (projectiveSpaceAtUniverse.{u} n)) = f ∧
        ∀ i, (nvCover s i).ι ≫ p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse n S =
          toProjectiveSpaceAtUniverse (chartRatio s i) (span_range_chartRatio s i) := by
  obtain ⟨N, n, s, hN, hgen, haff⟩ := exists_generating_family_of_isAmple L hL
  obtain ⟨p, hpf, hchart⟩ :=
    Stacks.ProjGlobalSectionsAppTop.exists_hom_projectiveSpaceOver_of_generatesStalks s hgen f
  exact ⟨N, n, s, p, hN, hgen, haff, hpf, hchart⟩

end Morphism

/-! ### The finite type hypothesis of Tag 01VS is necessary -/

section Necessity

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.DivisorCluster

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (M : X.Modules)

/-- **Tag 01VS's conclusion at a single degree implies Tag 01VS's own finite type hypothesis.** If
some `𝒪_X`-module is the hyperplane sheaf pulled back along an immersion `i : X ⟶ ℙⁿ_S` lying over
`S`, then `f` is locally of finite type, being that immersion followed by the structure morphism
of `ℙⁿ_S`.

So no reduction of Tag 01VS may drop the finite type hypothesis: a condition asserting
`HasImmersionTwistOver f M` for an unrestricted `f` is false for every `f` that is not locally of
finite type and that carries one invertible module with a generating family of global
sections. -/
theorem locallyOfFiniteType_of_hasImmersionTwistOver (h : HasImmersionTwistOver f M) :
    LocallyOfFiniteType f := by
  obtain ⟨n, i, hi, hif, -⟩ := h
  have : IsImmersion i := hi
  have := locallyOfFiniteType_terminal_from_projectiveSpaceAtUniverse.{u} n
  rw [← hif]
  exact MorphismProperty.comp_mem @LocallyOfFiniteType _ _ inferInstance inferInstance

end Necessity

/-! ### The named inputs -/

section Inputs

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (L : X.Modules)
  [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- **The twist identification of Stacks Tag 01NE.** A morphism `p : X ⟶ ℙⁿ_S` lying over `S` and
restricting on each chart `X_{sᵢ}` to the chart morphism attached to a generating family `s` of
global sections of an invertible `M` pulls the hyperplane sheaf back to `M`.

This is the half of Constructions, Lemma 27.13.1 that
`Stacks.ProjGlobalSectionsAppTop.exists_hom_projectiveSpaceOver_of_generatesStalks` does not
assert: that statement gives the morphism, pinned on every chart, and says nothing about `𝒪(1)`.

No ampleness, no finite type hypothesis, no immersion and no tensor power occurs in it. -/
def TwistPullback : Prop :=
  ∀ (M : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X M] (n : ℕ) (s : Fin (n + 1) → Γ(M, ⊤)),
    GeneratesStalks s → ∀ p : X ⟶ projectiveSpaceOver n S,
      p ≫ pullback.fst (terminal.from S)
          (terminal.from (projectiveSpaceAtUniverse.{u} n)) = f →
        (∀ i, (nvCover s i).ι ≫ p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse n S =
          toProjectiveSpaceAtUniverse (chartRatio s i) (span_range_chartRatio s i)) →
        Nonempty (M ≅ (Scheme.Modules.pullback p).obj (projectiveSpaceTwistingSheaf n S))

/-- **Steps 2 and 4 of the proof of Stacks Tag 01VS.** For an ample `L` on a scheme locally of
finite type over `S`, some positive power of `L` carries a generating family of global sections
whose pinned morphism to projective space over `S` is an immersion.

This is the geometric content the source obtains from the finite type hypothesis: on each chart
`X_{sᵢ}` the ring map from the affine chart `D₊(Tᵢ)` of `ℙⁿ_S` is surjective, because the
coordinate ratios `s_k / sᵢ` can be arranged to include the algebra generators of `𝒪_X(X_{sᵢ})`
over `𝒪_S(V_i)` produced by Stacks Tag 01T2 and written as ratios by Stacks Tag 01PW. Arranging
that is what fixes the degree: the `N` here is a common multiple of the degrees of the covering
elements and of the numerators Tag 01PW returns.

Step 2 writes a *function* on the chart as a ratio of two sections of powers of `L`, which is
Tag 01PW at `𝓕 = 𝒪_X`, proved from ampleness as
`Stacks.SectionExtension.isSectionRatio_of_isAmple` with denominator an arbitrary section with
`X_{a_i} ≤ X_σ` rather than a power of `a_i`. The module-valued form of Tag 01PW is what clause (5)
of Tag 01Q3 needs, hence what step 5 needs, and not this step.

It says nothing about `𝒪(1)`, and nothing about any degree beyond the single one it produces. -/
def ChartImmersion : Prop :=
  Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L → LocallyOfFiniteType f →
    ∃ (N : ℤ) (n : ℕ) (s : Fin (n + 1) → Γ(tensorPowModule X L N, ⊤)),
      1 ≤ N ∧ GeneratesStalks s ∧
        ∀ p : X ⟶ projectiveSpaceOver n S,
          p ≫ pullback.fst (terminal.from S)
              (terminal.from (projectiveSpaceAtUniverse.{u} n)) = f →
            (∀ i, (nvCover s i).ι ≫ p ≫ projectiveSpaceOver.toIntegralAtUniverse n S =
              toProjectiveSpaceAtUniverse (chartRatio s i) (span_range_chartRatio s i)) →
            IsImmersion p

/-- **Steps 6 and 7 of the proof of Stacks Tag 01VS: the Segre passage.** If `L ^⊗ a` is the
hyperplane sheaf pulled back along an immersion into projective space over `S`, and `L ^⊗ b` is
generated by finitely many global sections, then `L ^⊗ (a + b)` is again such a pullback.

The source proves this by multiplying the two families of sections, factoring the resulting
morphism as the pair `(j, j')` into `ℙᵐ_S ×_S ℙᵗ_S` followed by the Segre embedding, and using
that the pair is an immersion as soon as `j` is
(`Stacks.AmpleProjectiveImmersion.isImmersion_lift`) and that the Segre embedding is a closed
immersion (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreProdIso.exists_segreEmbedding`). Neither of those
asserts the identification of `𝒪(1)` along the Segre embedding.

No ampleness, no finite type hypothesis and no degree bound occurs in it, and it moves one degree
at a time. -/
def TwistPassage : Prop :=
  ∀ a b : ℤ, HasImmersionTwistOver f (tensorPowModule X L a) →
    Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen (tensorPowModule X L b) →
      HasImmersionTwistOver f (tensorPowModule X L (a + b))

end Inputs

/-! ### Stacks Tag 01VS from the named inputs -/

section Reduction

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- **Stacks Tag 01VS at a single degree**, from `TwistPullback` and `ChartImmersion`. The
morphism is the one of step 3; `ChartImmersion` says it is an immersion and `TwistPullback` says
it carries the hyperplane sheaf to the power.

The source remarks that this form of the conclusion "is enough in virtually all applications";
the passage to *every* `d ≥ d₀` is what needs the other two inputs. -/
theorem hasImmersionTwistOver_of_isAmple (htw : TwistPullback f) (hch : ChartImmersion f L)
    (hL : IsAmple X L) (hft : LocallyOfFiniteType f) :
    ∃ N : ℤ, 1 ≤ N ∧ HasImmersionTwistOver f (tensorPowModule X L N) := by
  obtain ⟨N, n, s, hN, hgen, himm⟩ := hch hL hft
  obtain ⟨p, hpf, hchart⟩ :=
    Stacks.ProjGlobalSectionsAppTop.exists_hom_projectiveSpaceOver_of_generatesStalks s hgen f
  exact ⟨N, hN, n, p, himm p hpf hchart, hpf, htw _ n s hgen p hpf hchart⟩

/-- **Tag 01VS in every degree `N + d k`, from three of the four inputs** — the fourth,
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers`, is not used.

`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule` gets one positive degree `d` with
`L ^⊗ d` generated by finitely many global sections out of ampleness alone, and `TwistPassage`
adds that degree repeatedly to the single degree `N` of `ChartImmersion`. So the conclusion of Tag
01VS holds on an arithmetic progression of degrees without the fourth input, which is needed
exactly for the remaining residue classes modulo `d`, as in the source. -/
theorem hasImmersionTwistOver_multiples_of_isAmple (htw : TwistPullback f)
    (hch : ChartImmersion f L) (hpass : TwistPassage f L) (hL : IsAmple X L)
    (hft : LocallyOfFiniteType f) :
    ∃ N d : ℤ, 1 ≤ N ∧ 1 ≤ d ∧
      ∀ k : ℕ, HasImmersionTwistOver f (tensorPowModule X L (N + d * (k : ℤ))) := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN, htwist⟩ := hasImmersionTwistOver_of_isAmple f L htw hch hL hft
  obtain ⟨d, hd, hfg⟩ := Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule L hL
  refine ⟨N, (d : ℤ), hN, by exact_mod_cast hd, fun k => ?_⟩
  induction k with
  | zero => simpa using htwist
  | succ k ih =>
    have key := hpass (N + (d : ℤ) * (k : ℤ)) (d : ℤ) ih hfg
    rw [show N + (d : ℤ) * (k : ℤ) + (d : ℤ) = N + (d : ℤ) * ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) from by
      push_cast; ring] at key
    exact key

/-- **The whole of `Stacks.AmpleProjectiveImmersion.ImmersionTwistGap` from the four named
inputs**, hence — through
`Stacks.AmpleProjectiveImmersion.exists_immersion_projectiveSpaceOver_of_isAmple'` and
`Stacks.PowerFamilyBridge.immersionTwistGap_iff` — the whole of Stacks Tag 01VS.

The bound is `d₀ = N + n₀`, with `N` the single degree of `ChartImmersion` and `n₀` the bound of
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers`, which is exactly the source's
`d₀ = d₁ + d₂`. Ampleness and the finite type hypothesis enter through `ChartImmersion`, and the
remaining two inputs carry the conclusion from the one degree `N` to every `d ≥ d₀`. -/
theorem immersionTwistGap_of_chartImmersionTwist (htw : TwistPullback f)
    (hch : ChartImmersion f L)
    (hpow : Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers X L)
    (hpass : TwistPassage f L) :
    ImmersionTwistGap f L (tensorPowModule X L) := by
  intro hL hft
  obtain ⟨N, hN, htwist⟩ := hasImmersionTwistOver_of_isAmple f L htw hch hL hft
  obtain ⟨n₀, hn₀⟩ := hpow
  have hNcast : ((N.toNat : ℤ)) = N := Int.toNat_of_nonneg (by linarith)
  have hn₀cast : n₀ ≤ (n₀.toNat : ℤ) := Int.self_le_toNat n₀
  refine ⟨N.toNat + n₀.toNat, by omega, fun d hd => ?_⟩
  have hdz : ((N.toNat : ℤ)) + (n₀.toNat : ℤ) ≤ (d : ℤ) := by exact_mod_cast hd
  have hb : n₀ ≤ (d : ℤ) - N := by omega
  have key := hpass N ((d : ℤ) - N) htwist (hn₀ _ hb)
  rw [show N + ((d : ℤ) - N) = (d : ℤ) from by ring] at key
  exact (hasImmersionTwist_iff f _).mpr key

/-- **Stacks Tag 01VS**, from the four named inputs
`Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.TwistPullback`, `Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.ChartImmersion`,
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers` and
`Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction.TwistPassage`.

The tensor powers are the ampleness theory's own, `Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule`, and
`Stacks.PowerFamilyBridge.tensorPowerModuleIso` identifies them with Stacks Tag 01CU's in every
integer degree. -/
theorem exists_immersion_projectiveSpaceOver_of_isAmple (hL : IsAmple X L)
    [hf : LocallyOfFiniteType f] (htw : TwistPullback f) (hch : ChartImmersion f L)
    (hpow : Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers X L)
    (hpass : TwistPassage f L) :
    ∃ d₀ : ℕ, 1 ≤ d₀ ∧ ∀ d : ℕ, d₀ ≤ d →
      ∃ (n : ℕ) (i : X ⟶ projectiveSpaceOver n S),
        IsImmersion i ∧
        i ≫ pullback.fst (terminal.from S)
          (terminal.from (projectiveSpaceAtUniverse.{u} n)) = f ∧
        Nonempty (tensorPowModule X L (d : ℤ) ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback i).obj (projectiveSpaceTwistingSheaf n S)) :=
  exists_immersion_projectiveSpaceOver_of_isAmple' f L hL
    (immersionTwistGap_of_chartImmersionTwist f L htw hch hpow hpass)

end Reduction

end Stacks.AmpleImmersionReduction

end
